---@field dynamicRetrievalConfig? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1DynamicRetrievalConfig Specifies the dynamic retrieval configuration for the given source.

---A piece of evidence that supports a claim made by the model. This is used to show a citation for a claim made by the model. When grounding is enabled, the model returns a `GroundingChunk` that contains a reference to the source of the information.
---@class gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GroundingChunk
---@field retrievedContext? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GroundingChunkRetrievedContext A grounding chunk from a data source retrieved by a retrieval tool, such as Vertex AI Search. See the `RetrievedContext` message for details
---@field maps? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GroundingChunkMaps A grounding chunk from Google Maps. See the `Maps` message for details.
---@field web? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GroundingChunkWeb A grounding chunk from a web page, typically from Google Search. See the `Web` message for details.
---@field image? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GroundingChunkImage A grounding chunk from an image search result. See the `Image` message for details.

---An `Image` chunk is a piece of evidence that comes from an image search result. It contains the URI of the image search result and the URI of the image. This is used to provide the user with a link to the source of the information.
---@class gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GroundingChunkImage
---@field imageUri? string The URI of the image.
---@field title? string The title of the image search result page.
---@field domain? string The domain of the image search result page.
---@field sourceUri? string The URI of the image search result page.

---@alias gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GroundingChunkList gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GroundingChunk[]

---A `Maps` chunk is a piece of evidence that comes from Google Maps, containing information about places or routes. This is used to provide the user with rich, location-based information.
