---@field encodedPolyline? string An encoded polyline of the route. See https://developers.google.com/maps/documentation/utilities/polylinealgorithm
---@field distanceMeters? number The total distance of the route, in meters.
---@field duration? string The total duration of the route.

---Context retrieved from a data source to ground the model's response. This is used when a retrieval tool fetches information from a user-provided corpus or a public dataset.
---@class gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GroundingChunkRetrievedContext
---@field text? string The content of the retrieved data source.
---@field uri? string The URI of the retrieved data source.
---@field documentName? string Output only. The full resource name of the referenced Vertex AI Search document. This is used to identify the specific document that was retrieved. The format is `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/dataStores/{data_store}/branches/{branch}/documents/{document}`.
---@field title? string The title of the retrieved data source.
---@field ragChunk? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RagChunk Additional context for a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) retrieval result. This is populated only when the RAG retrieval tool is used.

---A `Web` chunk is a piece of evidence that comes from a web page. It contains the URI of the web page, the title of the page, and the domain of the page. This is used to provide the user with a link to the source of the information.
---@class gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GroundingChunkWeb
---@field uri? string The URI of the web page that contains the evidence.
---@field title? string The title of the web page that contains the evidence.
---@field domain? string The domain of the web page that contains the evidence. This can be used to filter out low-quality sources.

---Information about the sources that support the content of a response. When grounding is enabled, the model returns citations for claims in the response. This object contains the retrieved sources.
---@class gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GroundingMetadata
---@field searchEntryPoint? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SearchEntryPoint Optional. A web search entry point that can be used to display search results. This field is populated only when the grounding source is Google Search.
---@field webSearchQueries? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.StringList Optional. The web search queries that were used to generate the content. This field is populated only when the grounding source is Google Search.
---@field groundingChunks? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GroundingChunkList A list of supporting references retrieved from the grounding source. This field is populated when the grounding source is Google Search, Vertex AI Search, or Google Maps.
---@field sourceFlaggingUris? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GroundingMetadataSourceFlaggingUriList Optional. Output only. A list of URIs that can be used to flag a place or review for inappropriate content. This field is populated only when the grounding source is Google Maps.
---@field groundingSupports? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GroundingSupportList Optional. A list of grounding supports that connect the generated content to the grounding chunks. This field is populated when the grounding source is Google Search or Vertex AI Search.
---@field retrievalMetadata? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1RetrievalMetadata Optional. Output only. Metadata related to the retrieval grounding source.
---@field retrievalQueries? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.StringList Optional. The queries that were executed by the retrieval tools. This field is populated only when the grounding source is a retrieval tool, such as Vertex AI Search.
---@field imageSearchQueries? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.StringList Optional. The image search queries that were used to generate the content. This field is populated only when the grounding source is Google Search with the Image Search search_type enabled.
---@field googleMapsWidgetContextToken? string Optional. Output only. Deprecated: The Google Maps contextual widget behavior in Grounding with Google Maps is being deprecated; this field is planned for removal and will no longer be populated once removed. A token that can be used to render a Google Maps widget with the contextual data. This field is populated only when the grounding source is Google Maps.

---A URI that can be used to flag a place or review for inappropriate content. This is populated only when the grounding source is Google Maps.
---@class gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GroundingMetadataSourceFlaggingUri
---@field flagContentUri? string The URI that can be used to flag the content.
---@field sourceId? string The ID of the place or review.

---@alias gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GroundingMetadataSourceFlaggingUriList gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GroundingMetadataSourceFlaggingUri[]

---A collection of supporting references for a segment or part of the model's response.
---@class gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GroundingSupport
---@field renderedParts? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.IntegerList Indices into the `rendered_parts` field of the `GroundingMetadata` message. These indices specify which rendered parts are associated with this support message.
---@field confidenceScores? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.DoubleList The confidence scores for the support references. This list is parallel to the `grounding_chunk_indices` list. A score is a value between 0.0 and 1.0, with a higher score indicating a higher confidence that the reference supports the claim. For Gemini 2.0 and before, this list has the same size as `grounding_chunk_indices`. For Gemini 2.5 and later, this list is empty and should be ignored.
---@field groundingChunkIndices? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.IntegerList A list of indices into the `grounding_chunks` field of the `GroundingMetadata` message. These indices specify which grounding chunks support the claim made in the content segment. For example, if this field has the values `[1, 3]`, it means that `grounding_chunks[1]` and `grounding_chunks[3]` are the sources for the claim in the content segment.
---@field segment? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Segment The content segment that this support message applies to.

---@alias gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GroundingSupportList gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GroundingSupport[]

---Configuration for image generation. This message allows you to control various aspects of image generation, such as the output format, aspect ratio, and whether the model can generate images of people.
---@class gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImageConfig
---@field prominentPeople? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImageConfigProminentPeopleEnum|string Optional. Controls whether prominent people (celebrities) generation is allowed. If used with personGeneration, personGeneration enum would take precedence. For instance, if ALLOW_NONE is set, all person generation would be blocked. If this field is unspecified, the default behavior is to allow prominent people.
---@field imageOutputOptions? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImageConfigImageOutputOptions Optional. The image output format for generated images.
---@field personGeneration? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImageConfigPersonGenerationEnum|string Optional. Controls whether the model can generate people.
---@field aspectRatio? string Optional. The desired aspect ratio for the generated images. The following aspect ratios are supported: "1:1" "2:3", "3:2" "3:4", "4:3" "4:5", "5:4" "9:16", "16:9" "21:9"
---@field imageSize? string Optional. Specifies the size of generated images. Supported values are `1K`, `2K`, `4K`. If not specified, the model will use default value `1K`.

---The image output format for generated images.
---@class gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImageConfigImageOutputOptions
---@field mimeType? string Optional. The image format that the output should be saved as.
---@field compressionQuality? number Optional. The compression quality of the output image.

---@alias gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImageConfigPersonGenerationEnum "PERSON_GENERATION_UNSPECIFIED"|"ALLOW_ALL"|"ALLOW_ADULT"|"ALLOW_NONE"

---@alias gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImageConfigProminentPeopleEnum "PROMINENT_PEOPLE_UNSPECIFIED"|"ALLOW_PROMINENT_PEOPLE"|"BLOCK_PROMINENT_PEOPLE"

---Configuration for image-specific output formatting.
---@class gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImageResponseFormat
---@field mimeType? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImageResponseFormatMimeTypeEnum|string Optional. The MIME type of the image output.
---@field delivery? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImageResponseFormatDeliveryEnum|string Optional. Delivery mode for the generated content.
---@field aspectRatio? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImageResponseFormatAspectRatioEnum|string Optional. The aspect ratio for the image output.
---@field imageSize? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImageResponseFormatImageSizeEnum|string Optional. The size of the image output.

---@alias gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImageResponseFormatAspectRatioEnum "ASPECT_RATIO_UNSPECIFIED"|"ASPECT_RATIO_ONE_BY_ONE"|"ASPECT_RATIO_TWO_BY_THREE"|"ASPECT_RATIO_THREE_BY_TWO"|"ASPECT_RATIO_THREE_BY_FOUR"|"ASPECT_RATIO_FOUR_BY_THREE"|"ASPECT_RATIO_FOUR_BY_FIVE"|"ASPECT_RATIO_FIVE_BY_FOUR"|"ASPECT_RATIO_NINE_BY_SIXTEEN"|"ASPECT_RATIO_SIXTEEN_BY_NINE"|"ASPECT_RATIO_TWENTY_ONE_BY_NINE"|"ASPECT_RATIO_ONE_BY_EIGHT"|"ASPECT_RATIO_EIGHT_BY_ONE"|"ASPECT_RATIO_ONE_BY_FOUR"|"ASPECT_RATIO_FOUR_BY_ONE"

---@alias gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImageResponseFormatDeliveryEnum "DELIVERY_UNSPECIFIED"|"INLINE"|"URI"

---@alias gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImageResponseFormatImageSizeEnum "IMAGE_SIZE_UNSPECIFIED"|"IMAGE_SIZE_FIVE_TWELVE"|"IMAGE_SIZE_ONE_K"|"IMAGE_SIZE_TWO_K"|"IMAGE_SIZE_FOUR_K"

---@alias gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ImageResponseFormatMimeTypeEnum "MIME_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"IMAGE_JPEG"

---The log probabilities of the tokens generated by the model. This is useful for understanding the model's confidence in its predictions and for debugging. For example, you can use log probabilities to identify when the model is making a less confident prediction or to explore alternative responses that the model considered. A low log probability can also indicate that the model is "hallucinating" or generating factually incorrect information.
---@class gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LogprobsResult
---@field chosenCandidates? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LogprobsResultCandidateList A list of the chosen candidate tokens at each decoding step. The length of this list is equal to the total number of decoding steps. Note that the chosen candidate might not be in `top_candidates`.
---@field topCandidates? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LogprobsResultTopCandidatesList A list of the top candidate tokens at each decoding step. The length of this list is equal to the total number of decoding steps.

---A single token and its associated log probability.
---@class gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LogprobsResultCandidate
---@field logProbability? number The log probability of this token. A higher value indicates that the model was more confident in this token. The log probability can be used to assess the relative likelihood of different tokens and to identify when the model is uncertain.
---@field tokenId? number The token's numerical ID. While the `token` field provides the string representation of the token, the `token_id` is the numerical representation that the model uses internally. This can be useful for developers who want to build custom logic based on the model's vocabulary.
---@field token? string The token's string representation.

---@alias gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LogprobsResultCandidateList gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LogprobsResultCandidate[]

---A list of the top candidate tokens and their log probabilities at each decoding step. This can be used to see what other tokens the model considered.
---@class gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LogprobsResultTopCandidates
---@field candidates? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LogprobsResultCandidateList The list of candidate tokens, sorted by log probability in descending order.

---@alias gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LogprobsResultTopCandidatesList gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1LogprobsResultTopCandidates[]

---Represents a breakdown of token usage by modality. This message is used in CountTokensResponse and GenerateContentResponse.UsageMetadata to provide a detailed view of how many tokens are used by each modality (e.g., text, image, video) in a request. This is particularly useful for multimodal models, allowing you to track and manage token consumption for billing and quota purposes.
---@class gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModalityTokenCount
---@field modality? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModalityTokenCountModalityEnum The modality that this token count applies to.
---@field tokenCount? number The number of tokens counted for this modality.

---@alias gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModalityTokenCountList gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModalityTokenCount[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModalityTokenCountModalityEnum "MODALITY_UNSPECIFIED"|"TEXT"|"IMAGE"|"VIDEO"|"AUDIO"|"DOCUMENT"

---Configuration for Model Armor. Model Armor is a Google Cloud service that provides safety and security filtering for prompts and responses. It helps protect your AI applications from risks such as harmful content, sensitive data leakage, and prompt injection attacks.
---@class gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ModelArmorConfig
---@field promptTemplateName? string Optional. The resource name of the Model Armor template to use for prompt screening. A Model Armor template is a set of customized filters and thresholds that define how Model Armor screens content. If specified, Model Armor will use this template to check the user's prompt for safety and security risks before it is sent to the model. The name must be in the format `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/templates/{template}`.
---@field responseTemplateName? string Optional. The resource name of the Model Armor template to use for response screening. A Model Armor template is a set of customized filters and thresholds that define how Model Armor screens content. If specified, Model Armor will use this template to check the model's response for safety and security risks before it is returned to the user. The name must be in the format `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/templates/{template}`.

---Configuration for a multi-speaker text-to-speech request.
---@class gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1MultiSpeakerVoiceConfig
---@field speakerVoiceConfigs? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SpeakerVoiceConfigList Required. A list of configurations for the voices of the speakers. Exactly two speaker voice configurations must be provided.

---A datatype containing media that is part of a multi-part Content message. A `Part` consists of data which has an associated datatype. A `Part` must contain one of the accepted types in `Part.data`. For media types that are not text, `Part` must have a fixed IANA MIME type identifying the type and subtype of the media if `inline_data` or `file_data` field is filled with raw bytes.
---@class gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Part
---@field codeExecutionResult? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1CodeExecutionResult Optional. The result of executing the ExecutableCode.
---@field fileData? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FileData Optional. The URI-based data of the part. This can be used to include files from Google Cloud Storage.
---@field mediaProcessing? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PartMediaProcessingEnum|string Optional. How the model processes this part's media for understanding. Only meaningful for video parts (`inline_data` or `file_data` with video mime). Non-video parts ignore this field.
---@field speechMetadata? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SpeechMetadata Optional. Turn-level metadata for speech generation (e.g. Daikon speaker/style). May be set alongside `text` to attach speaker and style information to a text part.
---@field inlineData? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Blob Optional. The inline data content of the part. This can be used to include images, audio, or video in a request.
---@field functionCall? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FunctionCall Optional. A predicted function call returned from the model. This contains the name of the function to call and the arguments to pass to the function.
---@field mediaResolution? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PartMediaResolution per part media resolution. Media resolution for the input media.
---@field executableCode? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1ExecutableCode Optional. Code generated by the model that is intended to be executed.
---@field videoMetadata? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1VideoMetadata Optional. Video metadata. The metadata should only be specified while the video data is presented in inline_data or file_data.
---@field functionResponse? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1FunctionResponse Optional. The result of a function call. This is used to provide the model with the result of a function call that it predicted.
---@field thought? boolean Optional. Indicates whether the `part` represents the model's thought process or reasoning.
---@field text? string Optional. The text content of the part. When sent from the VSCode Gemini Code Assist extension, references to @mentioned items will be converted to markdown boldface text. For example `@my-repo` will be converted to and sent as `**my-repo**` by the IDE agent.
---@field audioTranscription? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AudioTranscription Optional. Audio (input or output) transcription. This is only set when this `Part` contains audio data.
---@field thoughtSignature? string Optional. An opaque signature for the thought so it can be reused in subsequent requests.

---@alias gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PartList gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Part[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PartMediaProcessingEnum "MEDIA_PROCESSING_UNSPECIFIED"|"STATIC"|"AGENTIC"

---per part media resolution. Media resolution for the input media.
---@class gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PartMediaResolution
---@field level? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1PartMediaResolutionLevelEnum|string The tokenization quality used for given media.

