---Defines the schema of input and output data. This is a subset of the [OpenAPI 3.0 Schema Object](https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.0.3#schema-object).
---@class gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Schema
---@field default? any Optional. Default value to use if the field is not specified.
---@field maxLength? string Optional. If type is `STRING`, `max_length` specifies the maximum length of the string.
---@field title? string Optional. Title for the schema.
---@field defs? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SchemaMap Optional. `defs` provides a map of schema definitions that can be reused by `ref` elsewhere in the schema. Only allowed at root level of the schema.
---@field minProperties? string Optional. If type is `OBJECT`, `min_properties` specifies the minimum number of properties that can be provided.
---@field description? string Optional. Describes the data. The model uses this field to understand the purpose of the schema and how to use it. It is a best practice to provide a clear and descriptive explanation for the schema and its properties here, rather than in the prompt.
---@field required? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.StringList Optional. If type is `OBJECT`, `required` lists the names of properties that must be present.
---@field minimum? number Optional. If type is `INTEGER` or `NUMBER`, `minimum` specifies the minimum allowed value.
---@field maximum? number Optional. If type is `INTEGER` or `NUMBER`, `maximum` specifies the maximum allowed value.
---@field ref? string Optional. Allows referencing another schema definition to use in place of this schema. The value must be a valid reference to a schema in `defs`. For example, the following schema defines a reference to a schema node named "Pet": type: object properties: pet: ref: #/defs/Pet defs: Pet: type: object properties: name: type: string The value of the "pet" property is a reference to the schema node named "Pet". See details in https://json-schema.org/understanding-json-schema/structuring
---@field format? string Optional. The format of the data. For `NUMBER` type, format can be `float` or `double`. For `INTEGER` type, format can be `int32` or `int64`. For `STRING` type, format can be `email`, `byte`, `date`, `date-time`, `password`, and other formats to further refine the data type.
---@field maxItems? string Optional. If type is `ARRAY`, `max_items` specifies the maximum number of items in an array.
---@field anyOf? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SchemaList Optional. The instance must be valid against any (one or more) of the subschemas listed in `any_of`.
---@field enum? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.StringList Optional. Possible values of the field. This field can be used to restrict a value to a fixed set of values. To mark a field as an enum, set `format` to `enum` and provide the list of possible values in `enum`. For example: 1. To define directions: `{type:STRING, format:enum, enum:["EAST", "NORTH", "SOUTH", "WEST"]}` 2. To define apartment numbers: `{type:INTEGER, format:enum, enum:["101", "201", "301"]}`
---@field pattern? string Optional. If type is `STRING`, `pattern` specifies a regular expression that the string must match.
---@field additionalProperties? any Optional. If `type` is `OBJECT`, specifies how to handle properties not defined in `properties`. If it is a boolean `false`, no additional properties are allowed. If it is a schema, additional properties are allowed if they conform to the schema.
---@field minItems? string Optional. If type is `ARRAY`, `min_items` specifies the minimum number of items in an array.
---@field type? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SchemaTypeEnum|string Optional. Data type of the schema field.
---@field maxProperties? string Optional. If type is `OBJECT`, `max_properties` specifies the maximum number of properties that can be provided.
---@field example? any Optional. Example of an instance of this schema.
---@field minLength? string Optional. If type is `STRING`, `min_length` specifies the minimum length of the string.
---@field properties? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SchemaMap Optional. If type is `OBJECT`, `properties` is a map of property names to schema definitions for each property of the object.
---@field propertyOrdering? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.StringList Optional. Order of properties displayed or used where order matters. This is not a standard field in OpenAPI specification, but can be used to control the order of properties.
---@field items? gcp.unstable.firebaseml_v2beta.GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Schema Optional. If type is `ARRAY`, `items` specifies the schema of elements in the array.
---@field nullable? boolean Optional. Indicates if the value of this field can be null.

